"The Rapports are the knights' Privately Governed Territories; Rapport I is the first and largest."
"Rapport I is not the most populated, and has only one town, Root."
"The Rapport School near Root is a first school for all ages until university, with adult classes."
"Its summonarium receives people of the Triplanets and of worlds with Contracts."
"Its top library keeps students' study journals and chaos paintings of knights."
"Rapport I changes slowly, and humans had never before been seen there."
"Knight families of the und'h live in Rapport III."
"Parents can no longer donate children to the Rapports; a votary may still admit a child."
"Rapport School graduates must provide food, water, shelter and protection by magic."
"The standard: an adult wizard can keep a small village alive through a hard winter."
"First schools teach a blend of foraging and agricultural spells."
"Rapport I's burial ground lies past the hn'tyon's gate; each winter a few knights take their rest there."
"The Mother has seven Rapports; Rapport folk travel freely among them, sharing a culture."
"Rapport III, near the equator, is smaller than Rapport I but the most populous Rapport."
"Rapport III sits amid Artona I's most densely populated coastline; its city Wathe is full of votaries."
"Ancestral art'h trees link the Rapports; a few grow in Rapport III."
"The und'h are a renowned knight clan of Rapport III, more diverse than the art'h."
